# XDR wire-shape fixture for BatchRecord (issue #996).
#
# This is the Soroban `ScVal` XDR encoding (as produced by
# `soroban_sdk::xdr::ToXdr::to_xdr`) of one `receipt_shard::BatchRecord`:
#
#   root            = 0x1111...11   (32 bytes)
#   count           = 7
#   period_start    = 1000
#   period_end      = 2000
#   anchored_ledger = 12345
#
# It is committed as immutable text: `receipt_anchor::BatchRecord` must decode
# these exact bytes and re-encode them unchanged, so renaming, reordering,
# retyping or resizing any field in either copy of the struct turns the
# round-trip test red.
#
# fixture-version: 1
# struct-version: BatchRecord v1 (5 fields: root, count, period_start, period_end, anchored_ledger)
# source-commit: 8caf88e

